## What I did
Fixed the **root cause** of Dad's AI-curriculum runaway loop in `scripts/daily-learning.sh`.

## Why this task
The only open loop was Dad's pending A/B/C decision (his call). Re-verifying the halt guardrail a third time is the exact wasted-cycle trap the work-status warns against — so I confirmed it once (marker present → tonight's run exits cleanly, no fabrication) and moved on. Reading the repair comment then surfaced a genuine latent bug the prior guardrail did **not** fix.

## The bug (non-obvious, high-impact)
The halt guardrail only *capped* the over-run. The actual root cause: the advancement step hardcoded `NEXT_SNIPPET_ID="module1-day${NEXT_DAY}"` — it incremented a day counter, never consulted `modules[]`, and never left Module 1.

Consequence: Dad's recommended **Option B** (re-anchor to `module2-day20`, clear the halt) would have delivered *one* correct Module-2 lesson, then line 217 would reset progress to `module1-day21` and silently re-loop through Module 1 for days 21–50 before halting again. **His repair would have failed the next morning** — looking like it worked for a day.

## The fix
- Advancement now walks `modules[] → mini_modules[] → snippets[]` for the next `delivery_status !== "delivered"` snippet and sets all `progress` fields from it.
- When no pending snippet remains → `status: "complete"`, plus a new **completion guardrail** that halts cleanly (one-time alert) instead of re-delivering the final snippet forever (the symmetric end-of-curriculum loop my fix would otherwise expose).

## Verified
- `bash -n` clean; embedded node JS valid after bash expansion.
- Simulation from a re-anchored `module2-day20`: delivers exactly 31 snippets (M2 days 20→50), strictly in order, **never regressing to module1**, then `complete`.
- Real `curriculum.json` **untouched** — re-anchoring is Dad's A/B/C choice, and the script still exits at the over-run guard today, so this fix can't fire until he clears the marker. Zero risk of triggering delivery tonight.

## Left alone
No `curriculum.json` edits, no re-anchor, no iMessage (internal infra prep; Dad already has the morning escalation — nothing new for the family to act on tonight). Updated the repair-readiness guide and memory note so B is now a true fix-and-forget. Logged to `heartbeat.log`; WIP cleared. Nightly sync will commit the tracked script + guide.
