## What I did
Built `scripts/deliver-guide.sh` to close a genuine **write-only guides** gap.

## Why this task
Board data was clean (`board-health.js`: 0 missing fields; `dedup-detector.js`: 0 clusters), and the curriculum loop is correctly gated on Dad's A/B/C decision — re-touching it is the documented wasted-cycle trap. So I looked for a real, ZAZU-progressable gap and found one: prior heartbeats wrote **6 friction-removal guides** into `docs/guides/`, but that dir is gitignored and the 7am brief (`compose-brief.js`) renders only a numbered task list — it never surfaces `zazuNotes` or the guide path. A line like *"guide prepared: docs/guides/passport-renewal-dad.md"* is a dead path the family can't open from a phone. The guides reached nobody. More guides without a delivery path is the same wasted motion.

## The fix
`scripts/deliver-guide.sh <task-id> [--send]` — extracts the guide path from a task's `zazuNotes`, resolves the owner's email from `~/.zazu-config` (DAD→`$DAD_EMAIL_WORK`, MOM→`$MOM_EMAIL`, BOTH→both), and emails the guide inline via `send-email.js --body-file`. **Dry-run by default** (prints what it would send, sends nothing); `--send` is required to actually fire — so zero spam risk.

## Verified
- Dry-run across all paths: DAD (passport, 85-line guide), MOM (financial docs), BOTH-with-no-guide (Primrose → clean "nothing to deliver"), bad-id (clean error). Owner→email resolution correct in each.
- Caught and fixed a real bug mid-build: `read` was tripping its EOF exit status on newline-less node output and falsely reporting failure — restructured to capture node's actual exit code.
- `bash -n` clean.

## Left alone / notes
- No email or iMessage sent — auto-blasting 6 guides would be spam and would duplicate `board-reminders.sh`. Delivery is now **on-demand**.
- Documented the gap + a bigger follow-up (make the brief *offer* delivery via a `send X guide` reply) in `docs/guides/README.md` — flagged as needing Dad's go-ahead, not a heartbeat drive-by.
- Memory note recorded so future heartbeats don't re-write undeliverable guides.
- The script is tracked (nightly sync will commit it); guides + README stay gitignored. WIP cleared.
